<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- THE COMPANY'S OWN CONSOLE AND ITS OWN BENCH.

       Owner direction, 2026-10-06, naming both: "and the comms console and machining bench", after
       "rmeembr this might change the set gate option and stuff on doors".

       WHY THESE ARE A Building_CommsConsole AND A Building_WorkTable AND NOT PLAIN BUILDINGS.
       `CompRimroomsGateConsole` refuses to attach to a def whose thingClass is neither of those two
       - it has checked that since it was written - and the binding validator and the Operations
       pane both ask the same question. So the type IS the role test, which is why
       RimroomsGateProviders needs no def name to tell a console from a bench. Making these plain
       Buildings would have meant relaxing three separate checks to admit them, and every relaxed
       check is a hole somebody else can fall through.

       SO THE COMPANY CONSOLE IS A REAL COMMS CONSOLE, AND THAT IS A FEATURE RATHER THAN A SIDE
       EFFECT. `CorporateContact` already requires `console is Building_CommsConsole`, so the
       company's own console can hail the company, which is the one building where that reads as
       obvious. Register row 148 No Quests Without Comms is respected unchanged: its disposition is
       "configuration only; Rimrooms objectives must not depend on this quest filter", and nothing
       here depends on quests at all - the Operations contract board stays the separate board that
       card asks for.

       NEITHER REPLACES THE NATIVE ONE. Both are additions. A branch that never builds either keeps
       working exactly as it did, on Core's comms console and Core's machining table, which is what
       the reuse policy still requires of every bound role.

       AND BUILDING ONE CAN NEVER BREAK THE DOOR'S SET GATE BUTTON. That button binds a role only
       when it resolves unambiguously, so "one more candidate" would have meant a branch that built
       this console beside Core's suddenly being told RR_NativeGate_NoSingleConsole - the owner's own
       open 2026-10-03 report, caused by adding content. RimroomsGateProviders.Preferred gives
       exactly one of ours priority over any number of native ones, so building this can only ever
       resolve an ambiguity. -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>RR_GateConsole</defName>
    <label>company gate console</label>
    <thingClass>Building_CommsConsole</thingClass>
    <description>The console a company branch runs its gate from. It is a working comms console, so it hails the company and anyone else a standard set can reach, and it is built to be bound to a gate as that gate's control station.\n\nIt is smaller than a standard set and costs more to put up. A branch that has one does not need the standard set as well, and a branch that never builds one loses nothing: an ordinary comms console does the same job.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Rimrooms/RR_GateConsole</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(1.4,1.4)</drawSize>
      <damageData>
        <cornerTL>Damage/Corner</cornerTL>
        <cornerTR>Damage/Corner</cornerTR>
        <cornerBL>Damage/Corner</cornerBL>
        <cornerBR>Damage/Corner</cornerBR>
      </damageData>
    </graphicData>
    <size>(1,1)</size>
    <!-- NOT ROTATABLE, HONESTLY. The master is a front elevation with a clear face; there is no
         back view and no side view, and a Graphic_Multi carrying one frame is a missing-texture
         square on three facings. tools/cut-phase2-art.py lists this under ROTATIONS WANTED, and
         check-register-compliance.py rule 6b refuses the dishonest version. -->
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <hasInteractionCell>true</hasInteractionCell>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-1)</interactionCellOffset>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>50</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.5</fillPercent>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>140</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>2600</WorkToBuild>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-2</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>90</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>5</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <designationCategory>Misc</designationCategory>
    <designationHotKey>Misc9</designationHotKey>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Heavy</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <building>
      <paintable>false</paintable>
      <destroySound>BuildingDestroyed_Metal_Medium</destroySound>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Power">
        <compClass>CompPowerTrader</compClass>
        <basePowerConsumption>200</basePowerConsumption>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Flickable" />
      <!-- Declared here rather than patched in. The patch that adds this component to Core's
           CommsConsole and TableMachining is for defs we do not own; this one is ours. -->
      <li Class="RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Gate.CompProperties_RimroomsGateConsole" />
    </comps>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap</li>
    </placeWorkers>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BenchBase">
    <defName>RR_FieldAnalysisBench</defName>
    <label>field analysis bench</label>
    <thingClass>Building_WorkTable</thingClass>
    <description>A long analysis counter: a reel recorder, a reader and a terminal on one run of worktop. The company fits them in branch laboratories so gate assembly work and the examination of whatever comes back off a run happen at the same bench.\n\nIt can be bound to a gate as that gate's assembly bench. A branch that never builds one can bind an ordinary machining table instead and lose nothing.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Rimrooms/RR_FieldAnalysisBench</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,1)</drawSize>
      <damageData>
        <rect>(0,0.2,2,0.6)</rect>
      </damageData>
    </graphicData>
    <size>(2,1)</size>
    <!-- NOT ROTATABLE, for the same reason and a sharper one: a counter's end on view is a
         completely different drawing, and there is no master for it. -->
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <hasInteractionCell>true</hasInteractionCell>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-1)</interactionCellOffset>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>60</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.5</fillPercent>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>220</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>3200</WorkToBuild>
      <Mass>30</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-1</Beauty>
      <WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor>1</WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>120</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>6</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Machining</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <designationCategory>Production</designationCategory>
    <designationHotKey>Misc10</designationHotKey>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Heavy</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <!-- NO RECIPES, AND THAT IS A DECISION RATHER THAN AN OMISSION. Its job in this release is to
         be a gate's assembly bench, which is driven by the gate's assembly shares and not by a bill
         stack. Giving it Core's machining recipes would make it a better machining table, which is
         a balance change nobody asked for, and register row 53 Big Little Mod Patch records the
         mechanism that makes recipes additive later with no code naming them: "the bill work family
         reads its bench set from every loaded WorkGiverDef's fixedBillGiverDefs". -->
    <building>
      <paintable>false</paintable>
      <destroySound>BuildingDestroyed_Metal_Medium</destroySound>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Power">
        <compClass>CompPowerTrader</compClass>
        <basePowerConsumption>200</basePowerConsumption>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Flickable" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_Breakdownable" />
      <li Class="RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Gate.CompProperties_RimroomsGateConsole" />
      <!-- The bench has to name the facility back or the link never forms. One facility, Core's
           own mechanic, no new C#: a field recorder standing within six cells takes 12% off the
           bench's work. -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_AffectedByFacilities">
        <linkableFacilities>
          <li>RR_FieldRecorder</li>
        </linkableFacilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap</li>
      <li>PlaceWorker_ShowFacilitiesConnections</li>
    </placeWorkers>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
